[include version_include.man]
[manpage_begin ns_package_provenance n [vset version]]
[moddesc {NaviServer Built-in Commands}]
[titledesc {Inspect observed Tcl package loading provenance}]

[description]
NaviServer observes Tcl package requirements, explicit package registrations,
and packages registered by Tcl's native [cmd load] command. Records are shared
between interpreters of the current virtual server in the server-scoped NSV
array [const ns_package_provenance]. They are not copied into interpreter
blueprints. Tracking starts before server Tcl libraries are sourced and is
attached to subsequently allocated server interpreters.

[section COMMANDS]
[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ns_package_provenance] [const get] [arg package] [opt [arg version]]]
Return the provenance dict for the specified package/version, or an empty dict
when no record exists. With no version, use the provided version in the current
interpreter. This lookup never requires or initializes a package.

[para]
The dict has three fields:
[list_begin itemized]
[item] [const providedBy]: a list of observed Tcl source registrations or native
library providers. Native registrations already present when tracing attaches
have an explicit [const preexisting] origin; their original provider is unknown.
[item] [const requiredBy]: deduplicated successful [cmd {package require}]
call sites, including source file/line, procedure, version requirements and
[option -exact]. A package name in the origin identifies an enclosing loading
request. Calls outside a loading request retain their source location. Package-index discovery
can itself issue requirements; such an enclosing request is loading context,
not proof that its implementation directly uses the dependency.
[item] [const firstLoadedBy]: the first observed successful loading request, or
a direct registration site when no requirement was active. Already-present
packages are marked [const preexisting]. A provision made during a failed
loader is retained, but that failure is not attributed as a successful load.
[list_end]

[para]
Source origins have [const kind], [const file], [const line], [const proc] and
[const packages] fields. Native origins have [const kind], [const file] and
[const init]. Requirements additionally have [const requested] and [const exact].
A dynamic caller can have no source file. A package can have multiple providers,
including aliases registered while another package loads. Package versions are
recorded separately. Historical records remain after [cmd {package forget}].
[list_end]

[section {LIMITATIONS}]
Tracking records loading declarations, not execution of package commands.
Failed requirements do not add successful dependency edges. Operations which
occurred before observation cannot be reconstructed. Native registrations
which bypass Tcl's [cmd load] command may likewise have no observed provider.
Only interpreters initialized by this virtual server's normal lifecycle are
tracked; independent child interpreters must explicitly attach observation.

[para]
Blueprint updates suspend observation so copied registrations are not mistaken
for new loading events. The observer preserves package return/error behavior.
Only package/version identifiers, file locations and procedure names are
retained; command text and application argument values are not recorded.
The implementation uses execution traces on [cmd package], [cmd load], and
[cmd {ns_ictl update}], with short-lived per-interpreter nesting stacks stored
in shared NSVs and removed when empty.

[para]
Install the startup script and restart the server to enable startup provenance.
The Tcl Libraries page in nsstats shows the records for packages provided in
its current interpreter; it does not union package inventories across workers.

[see_also nsv ns_ictl tcl-lib-nstrace]
[keywords package provenance require provide interpreter]
[manpage_end]
